Z||000004||ChadMan||01-26-2001||09:11 AM||||There are some good laughs to be had over there...<P>"my friend raced an 87 GT with his stock 1997 cavalier z24.....newasy (???) we hit 150 km/h and he just seemed to fade in the distance.....i thinkthsoe (???) fieros top end are only 150 km/h....." (corey)<P>150 km/h = 93 mph.  I'd have to guess the 87 GT was capable of more than that.<P>"News for ya, plastic can't rust, therefore Fieros cant..." (mkskud)<P>Guess the space frame and cradle were plastic too.  Whew, what a relief!  Guess I can stop crawling under every Fiero I consider buying to check for rust damage.<P>"A stock Cavalier will out handle a stock Fiero SE..." (SandDemon)<P>Only if Michael Andretti is in the Cavvy and SandDemon's mother is driving the Fiero.<P>"well for all you people who don't like the fiero you are really stupid!" (xs speed)<P>Well put.  Hey, he said it, I didn't...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000005||COUNTIBLIS||01-26-2001||10:09 AM||||Author: BlownZ (---.sympatico.ca)<BR>Date:   01-07-01 18:29<P>In 1988 , when Pontiac was testing the 1989 Fiero's , The top brass from Gm came to take a look at there new little rocket . Tne 89 Fiero's were blowing the doors off the Corvette on the test track . We went to a fiero show in Michigan last summer with some friends that own a shop that modded Fiero's (RACETECH). <BR>The designer of the fiero was there and was telling us that the 89 Fiero was a twin turbo 3.1L that was out handling and out powering the Corvette . So the following weeks of the testing Gm Brass cancelled the Fiero and that plant became the Saturn Plant . <P>Just thought you would like to know.<P>This just bothers the hell out of me!  Damn the Corvette damn it to hell!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Black88GT||01-26-2001||10:27 AM||||HEY! thats me!  My friend's parents bought him a brand new Z24 and he referred me to that site. So I went over there out of curiousity's sake and I saw a couple Fiero posts.  One guy over there seems to be a pretty big enthusiast too, but didn't know about the forum so I told him about it, he said he would stop by.  I think the guy on here now asking about 85 GT's was over there also.<P>I think it is interesting how the message boards with mainly older members seems to be the most closed minded bunch.  I have talked about Fiero's in a Honda forum once (friend has B16A CRX) and they all liked it and said it was a shame GM stopped making them.  I talked about it in that j-body forum and most people had a good or atleast decent opinion on them.  Go over to the F-Body forum and watch the flames fly with a mere hint of the word Fiero....<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000007||RossT||01-26-2001||10:41 AM||||Would you have some links to these other car forums?  I really enjoy paging thru some of them!!<P>BTW It would have taken me the whole day to write your fiero response..  Good Job!!||||reg||1
Z||000008||ChadMan||01-26-2001||10:48 AM||||For the record, I like the J-bodies just fine, especially the old V6 Z24's and the new twin-cam Z24 and Sunfire GT.  They're quick and fun, and unlike the Fiero, they're pretty useful with a fair-sized back seat and trunk.<P>But the idea that a stock J-body will outhandle a stock Fiero is just silly.  And a new Z24 might be faster than a V6 Fiero, but not by much.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Black88GT||01-26-2001||10:58 AM||||I saw who it was, it was that guy Prophet.  He sounds like he could really benefit from a forum like this one.  We have to try and get him over here!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.honda-tech.com" TARGET=_blank>www.honda-tech.com</A>  is where I am "Fiero".  The board over there is wild, there are so many options.  Worth checking out.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.corvette-forum.com" TARGET=_blank>www.corvette-forum.com</A>  I am also "Fiero" over there, I haven't checked that in ages though, but most of the guys there flame Fiero's of course.  Older crowd...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.scca-forums.com" TARGET=_blank>www.scca-forums.com</A>  is a good autoX site.  Not to much happens over there however.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||p4n1c||01-26-2001||11:07 AM||||My dad loves Corvettes, and when he gets the money to do so will be restoring one, but I think he's pretty interested in me getting a Fiero.  He was asking me what I was going to do to the engine and stuff.  <P>So not all Corvette people are bad.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Nor are some F-Body people.  I know two and they are pretty interested in my Fiero after I showed them some of the mods and body kits and all that good stuff for them.  <P>For the most part with the younger crowd, even if they poke fun at the car, once you show them what you can do with it and how fun it is, they get pretty turned onto them.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>"Each passing day, every passing face seems like such a blur" <BR>- The Offspring(Million Miles Away)||||reg||1
Z||000011||rogergarrison||01-26-2001||12:23 PM||||I like wasting F-bodies on freeway, ate a Camaro last nite matter of fact on I-270. I have a bunch of friends who have all years Corvettes (Crossed Flags Corvettes of Columbus) I do lots of body and paint work for them and there all pretty cool. I travel with them on thier roadtrips too in my Ferrari replica whenever my clubs not doing anything. Out on backroads weve been known to play a little too, hehe. One guy has a 67 I think with the 427, havent been able to keep up with him ......yet. lol<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
